    <!-- Onboarding -->
    <string name="onboarding_title_1">Meet Oak</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_1">Oak is your private AI assistant that can control your phone — open apps, send texts, like posts, set alarms, and more.\n\nEvery action is governed by a trust kernel that keeps you in control. Let\'s get you set up.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_title_2">Enable Accessibility</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_2">Oak needs accessibility access to see your screen and perform actions like tapping, scrolling, and typing.\n\nAfter tapping the button below:\n\n1. Find \"Oak &amp; Sparrow\" in the list\n2. Tap it\n3. Toggle the switch ON\n4. Tap \"Allow\" on the confirmation dialog\n5. Come back to this app</string>
    <string name="onboarding_title_3">Notifications</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_3">Allow notifications so Oak can tell you when an action needs your approval, or show you what it\'s working on.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_title_4">Default Assistant</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_4">Make Oak your default assistant so you can launch it anytime by long-pressing the home button.\n\nIf a picker appears, select \"Oak &amp; Sparrow\". If it opens Settings instead:\n\n1. Tap \"Digital assistant app\"\n2. Select \"Oak &amp; Sparrow\"\n3. Come back to this app</string>
    <string name="onboarding_title_5">Display Over Apps</string>
    <string name="onboarding_body_5">Allow Oak to show its voice overlay on top of other apps. This lets you talk to Oak while using any app — just long-press home to bring it up.</string>
